# Git and worktree safety

## Protect existing work

- Never discard or rewrite uncommitted changes you did not create for this task
- Forbidden without explicit user request: `git reset --hard`, `git checkout --`, `git clean -fd`, `git stash` on foreign dirty trees
- Do not amend commits unless the user explicitly asks and amend rules are met
- No force push; no `--no-verify` unless explicitly requested

## Worktrees

- Prefer the assigned worktree; list `git worktree list` before creating another
- New worktrees need free disk check; abort if space is critical (use agent store for drafts)
- Do not start Homebrew DB services or alter other worktrees' PGDATA
- Keep unrelated dirty changes out of governance/docs commits (split commits/PRs)

## Integration policy

- Do not use the `automerge` label; do not enable repo auto-merge
- Production branch (`fix/login-localize-and-session-helper`) changes only with per-operation approval
- Prefer PR-based review for non-trivial changes
- Conventional Commits when committing is approved (`docs/CONVENTIONAL_COMMITS.md`)
- Ruleset blocks deletion and force-push on the production branch; policy forbids force-push everywhere
